1
00:00:09,153 --> 00:00:13,234
[Subtitles by danielsangeo]

2
00:00:15,217 --> 00:00:20,620
Okay, I've decided it's not safe here.
All this rock dust is a health hazard.

3
00:00:20,620 --> 00:00:23,246
I'm definitely not taking a nap here.

4
00:00:23,246 --> 00:00:28,320
At least I don't think that's natural gas
leaking in here. It doesn't smell like it.

5
00:00:28,320 --> 00:00:31,567
Hey, maybe it's ether! Mmm!

6
00:00:31,567 --> 00:00:34,781
Oh, this is helpful. That's very
considerate of the rock

7
00:00:34,781 --> 00:00:37,000
[plane whine, explosions]
not to completely crush the exit.

8
00:00:38,560 --> 00:00:40,146
The bombings are less helpful.

9
00:00:40,146 --> 00:00:41,706
RADIO: Forget about Freeman!
Wuahh...!

10
00:00:41,706 --> 00:00:44,063
RADIO: We are cutting our
losses and pulling out!

11
00:00:44,063 --> 00:00:46,723
RADIO: Anyone left down there
now is on his own!

12
00:00:46,723 --> 00:00:49,156
RADIO: Repeat: If you weren't
already, you're now--

13
00:00:49,156 --> 00:00:50,759
[explosion]
Hey, did you hear that?

14
00:00:50,759 --> 00:00:52,667
They said, "Forget about Freeman."

15
00:00:53,735 --> 00:00:56,801
Hey, I wonder if I can delete
myself as an employee.

16
00:00:58,727 --> 00:01:01,434
Probably not, but... no... This isn't--

17
00:01:01,885 --> 00:01:04,081
[gunshots]

18
00:01:04,081 --> 00:01:04,631
Uh-oh.

19
00:01:04,631 --> 00:01:06,310
[gunshots]

20
00:01:06,310 --> 00:01:07,170
[turret whirring down]

21
00:01:07,170 --> 00:01:10,234
That guard has no idea how lucky he is.

22
00:01:10,234 --> 00:01:13,346
Well, he was bright enough to start
shooting at it, I'll give him that.

23
00:01:13,346 --> 00:01:15,638
He's probably seen what these things do.

24
00:01:15,638 --> 00:01:19,846
Although, I have to say, I think this is
just a taste of what the future holds.

25
00:01:19,846 --> 00:01:22,714
Like, right now, if you walk in
the parking lot of Walmart,

26
00:01:22,714 --> 00:01:25,639
there are dozens of surveillance
cameras watching you.

27
00:01:25,639 --> 00:01:29,745
I think in, maybe 50 years, there will
also be roof-mounted turret guns

28
00:01:29,745 --> 00:01:32,094
in order to gun down shoplifters.

29
00:01:32,094 --> 00:01:34,226
Okay, Stumpy, you're my new bodyguard.

30
00:01:34,226 --> 00:01:36,077
GUARD: Roger that, let's run like hell!

31
00:01:36,077 --> 00:01:38,602
Well, see, that was my first impulse, too,

32
00:01:38,602 --> 00:01:41,404
but I would advise against
being a track star around here,

33
00:01:41,404 --> 00:01:43,974
what with all the lasers and
mines and death--

34
00:01:43,974 --> 00:01:44,901
[agrunt rumbles]
Hup!

35
00:01:46,207 --> 00:01:47,334
See what I mean?!

36
00:01:52,710 --> 00:01:54,816
Hey, I don't know how much
ammo you're carrying,

37
00:01:54,816 --> 00:01:57,028
but you can fire more shots than that.

38
00:01:57,028 --> 00:02:00,562
Those guys will crush our heads like
grapes if we don't take them down.

39
00:02:00,562 --> 00:02:01,665
Do you understand?

40
00:02:01,665 --> 00:02:05,334
Your helmet's not going to stop them.
It's giving you a false sense of security.

41
00:02:06,368 --> 00:02:08,833
I mean, look at this! Do you see this?

42
00:02:08,833 --> 00:02:10,400
Okay, try to keep up, alright?

43
00:02:10,670 --> 00:02:13,663
GUARD: Hey!
Shit... not this way...

44
00:02:13,663 --> 00:02:16,043
...the other way... with the... no, bees...

45
00:02:16,043 --> 00:02:17,452
[plane whines]
...less bees...

46
00:02:17,452 --> 00:02:18,963
[explosions]
...oh, more bombing! YES!

47
00:02:18,963 --> 00:02:20,801
NOW I'M COMPLETE! FUCK!

48
00:02:22,020 --> 00:02:23,500
I'M GETTING SANDWICHED!

49
00:02:25,980 --> 00:02:26,667
MOVE!

50
00:02:31,654 --> 00:02:33,334
This is such a busy day!

51
00:02:35,043 --> 00:02:36,434
[shudders]

52
00:02:37,123 --> 00:02:39,802
See, chess doesn't prepare you for this.

53
00:02:39,802 --> 00:02:42,976
You can't say that a rook and
three pawns flanked your knight,

54
00:02:42,976 --> 00:02:46,092
but he laid down suppressing fire
and punched through them anyway.

55
00:02:46,092 --> 00:02:48,517
You get disqualified if you try that.

56
00:02:48,517 --> 00:02:51,374
Maybe I've been disqualified from reality.

57
00:02:51,374 --> 00:02:52,956
I mean, what is THIS?

58
00:02:52,956 --> 00:02:54,367
This isn't real, is it?

59
00:02:55,632 --> 00:02:56,966
How can I know?

60
00:02:56,966 --> 00:03:01,014
It's too easy to just explain
all this away as aliens.

61
00:03:01,014 --> 00:03:03,432
It's aliens AND teleportation,

62
00:03:03,432 --> 00:03:05,473
and a conspiracy against me,

63
00:03:05,473 --> 00:03:06,634
and drugs,

64
00:03:06,634 --> 00:03:08,591
and in-house genocide,

65
00:03:08,591 --> 00:03:09,620
and ghosts,

66
00:03:09,620 --> 00:03:12,155
and now these cosmic disco balls.

67
00:03:12,155 --> 00:03:14,440
And I'm still hungry, dammit!

68
00:03:14,440 --> 00:03:17,330
Why don't the soldiers
carry any MREs on them?

69
00:03:17,330 --> 00:03:19,228
What the fuck?

70
00:03:19,228 --> 00:03:21,425
Alright, well,
mission accomplished, assholes,

71
00:03:21,425 --> 00:03:23,234
you make me not want to go this way.

72
00:03:24,074 --> 00:03:24,834
Ugh!

73
00:03:25,308 --> 00:03:31,275
Well, at best, this shit is harmless
like shed skin or something,

74
00:03:31,275 --> 00:03:36,961
at worst, I'm dead already
because of alien pathogens.

75
00:03:36,961 --> 00:03:38,968
Christ, another one.

76
00:03:39,514 --> 00:03:42,736
Although, I'm going to bet
on "safe" because I'm guessing

77
00:03:42,736 --> 00:03:46,837
our DNA is so different, the alien
viruses haven't had enough time

78
00:03:46,837 --> 00:03:49,652
to figure out what the hell
they're dealing with yet.

79
00:03:49,652 --> 00:03:51,806
Well, this is the only way.

80
00:03:51,806 --> 00:03:53,943
[snarks chirping]
Shit.

81
00:03:53,943 --> 00:03:56,036
[snarks chirping]
No... NO...!

82
00:03:56,036 --> 00:03:57,500
I'M NOT YOUR MOTHER!

83
00:03:58,535 --> 00:04:00,267
STOP IMPRINTING!

84
00:04:02,024 --> 00:04:03,200
DON'T FOLLOW ME!

85
00:04:04,663 --> 00:04:05,467
STOP IT!

86
00:04:06,070 --> 00:04:07,372
BLAAAAAAAAAAH!

87
00:04:08,119 --> 00:04:10,622
I wouldn't make a very good babysitter.

88
00:04:10,622 --> 00:04:13,383
I mean, my first impulse towards
seeing a bunch of kids run around

89
00:04:13,383 --> 00:04:15,288
is to throw things at them.

90
00:04:15,288 --> 00:04:17,067
I mean, not lethal or anything.

91
00:04:18,415 --> 00:04:20,707
God, how many of these things are there?

92
00:04:20,707 --> 00:04:23,733
So these are egg sac light shows.

93
00:04:23,733 --> 00:04:27,100
You know what? I'm me.
Let's be smart about this.

94
00:04:28,309 --> 00:04:29,853
Yeah, that's good.

95
00:04:29,853 --> 00:04:33,467
But yeah, wouldn't all these flashing
lights just attract predators?

96
00:04:33,467 --> 00:04:35,984
This seems like an evolutionary liability.

97
00:04:35,984 --> 00:04:36,534
Click!

98
00:04:38,930 --> 00:04:43,222
Okay, so what I'm seeing is NOT real.

99
00:04:43,222 --> 00:04:48,678
Either that or I've been tricked and these
are actually just very elaborate fireworks.

100
00:04:48,678 --> 00:04:52,706
And this thing is floating in
mid-air. That just now hit me.

101
00:04:52,706 --> 00:04:54,200
Let's be certain about this.

102
00:04:55,632 --> 00:04:57,749
[explosion, snarks chirping]

103
00:04:57,749 --> 00:05:00,145
Alright, so this IS real.

104
00:05:00,145 --> 00:05:00,767
Uh-oh.

105
00:05:02,107 --> 00:05:02,767
NO!

106
00:05:03,147 --> 00:05:04,400
I DON'T WANT YOU!

107
00:05:04,960 --> 00:05:05,601
STOP!

108
00:05:06,442 --> 00:05:09,872
Hey, what happened to that security guard
who was supposed to have my back?

109
00:05:09,872 --> 00:05:12,081
He's probably just screwing around...

110
00:05:12,081 --> 00:05:13,845
Well, I'm not going back for him.

111
00:05:13,845 --> 00:05:18,147
He was firing so slowly you'd think he
was loading black powder into the gun barrel

112
00:05:18,147 --> 00:05:19,475
between each shot.

113
00:05:19,475 --> 00:05:20,920
Maybe he reenacts battles--

114
00:05:20,920 --> 00:05:21,817
[agrunt rumbles]

115
00:05:24,175 --> 00:05:26,934
Why do I feel like
I'm fighting a dump truck?

116
00:05:28,994 --> 00:05:29,634
YAH!

117
00:05:30,945 --> 00:05:32,000
NNNNYAAA-AAAH!

118
00:05:33,573 --> 00:05:35,947
[agrunt moans]

119
00:05:35,947 --> 00:05:39,421
A howling dump truck full of... bees.

120
00:05:39,421 --> 00:05:41,842
It's all that armor they're
wearing, but it's weird

121
00:05:41,842 --> 00:05:46,844
because it shows off their obvious alien
pectoral muscles. That's not practical.

122
00:05:46,844 --> 00:05:49,863
That's the kind of armor a
male stripper would wear.

123
00:05:49,863 --> 00:05:52,102
Are we being invaded by strippers?

124
00:05:52,102 --> 00:05:55,391
I assumed this invasion was the
normal conquering variety,

125
00:05:55,391 --> 00:05:59,688
but maybe it has a
strange kinky alien context.

126
00:05:59,688 --> 00:06:01,467
Okay, one more try.

127
00:06:02,200 --> 00:06:05,828
[explosion, snarks chirp]
Yay! I win the nightmare piñata!

128
00:06:05,828 --> 00:06:08,120
These things shouldn't be out in the wild!

129
00:06:08,120 --> 00:06:11,919
We need to round them up for ring fights
like any civilized society would!

130
00:06:11,919 --> 00:06:13,695
You start with small animals...

131
00:06:13,695 --> 00:06:14,634
move up to big...

132
00:06:15,319 --> 00:06:15,734
Dammit!

133
00:06:16,407 --> 00:06:19,722
...then steadily increase the
odds for bet payouts!

134
00:06:19,722 --> 00:06:21,653
They seem to combust quickly, though.

135
00:06:21,653 --> 00:06:24,067
They must be reacting to
something in our atmosphere.

136
00:06:24,618 --> 00:06:25,642
Good!

137
00:06:25,642 --> 00:06:27,711
That's all I have to say about that.

138
00:06:27,711 --> 00:06:29,782
I hope there's something
valuable down here,

139
00:06:29,782 --> 00:06:32,740
[plane whine]
but what the aliens consider valuable--

140
00:06:32,740 --> 00:06:36,490
[explosion]
Christ! How am I not deep enough yet?!

141
00:06:36,490 --> 00:06:39,476
Anyway, they probably
consider slime mold valuable.

142
00:06:39,476 --> 00:06:40,434
[agrunt rumble]
AH!

143
00:06:41,696 --> 00:06:43,033
I'm here for the molds!

144
00:06:43,691 --> 00:06:44,834
And the fungus!

145
00:06:45,951 --> 00:06:47,635
I'VE GOT YOU PINNED DOWN!

146
00:06:47,635 --> 00:06:52,367
YOU'LL NEVER LEAVE WITH OUR MUSHROOMS, AND
OTHER CRAP THAT GROWS IN CELLARS, ALIVE!

147
00:06:55,813 --> 00:06:56,367
Ergh!

148
00:06:57,320 --> 00:06:59,434
AAARGH! FUCKING BEES!

149
00:07:00,590 --> 00:07:02,000
Why is there--WUAAH!

150
00:07:02,657 --> 00:07:05,195
Yeah, this is just a storage lockup.

151
00:07:05,195 --> 00:07:06,881
Okay, time for round two.

152
00:07:07,477 --> 00:07:08,143
Whoa!

153
00:07:09,331 --> 00:07:12,267
I wonder if he actually is just
guarding mushrooms.

154
00:07:12,267 --> 00:07:13,902
[teleportation sound]
What?

155
00:07:13,902 --> 00:07:14,741
WAH!

156
00:07:14,741 --> 00:07:17,500
JESUS CHRIST!
IT TELEPORTED RIGHT NEXT TO ME!

157
00:07:18,461 --> 00:07:21,247
THAT'S TOO CLOSE! THEY'RE GOING
TO TELEPORT INSIDE ME!

158
00:07:21,878 --> 00:07:22,567
NO!

159
00:07:23,577 --> 00:07:24,734
TIME TO RETREAT!

160
00:07:25,522 --> 00:07:26,067
WHAT?!

161
00:07:26,350 --> 00:07:27,895
WHY IS HE NOT DEAD YET?

162
00:07:27,895 --> 00:07:31,146
DO I HAVE TO KILL EVERYONE
AROUND HERE MYSELF?!

163
00:07:31,146 --> 00:07:32,234
GRAAAAARGH!

164
00:07:32,619 --> 00:07:34,000
Lead by example...

165
00:07:35,210 --> 00:07:37,307
I can't delegate anything.

166
00:07:37,307 --> 00:07:41,719
You know, being a one-man army isn't
actually something you aspire to.

167
00:07:41,719 --> 00:07:43,708
You say that because it sounds bad ass,

168
00:07:43,708 --> 00:07:47,199
not because you LITERALLY want
to function as an entire army!

169
00:07:47,199 --> 00:07:51,507
But, what are my options?! Do
everything myself or just die!

170
00:07:51,507 --> 00:07:54,996
My opinion of humanity is so low right now.

171
00:07:54,996 --> 00:07:57,701
Or maybe not humanity but... everything.

172
00:07:58,904 --> 00:08:01,100
Okay, let's play this game!

173
00:08:02,254 --> 00:08:05,033
Bet somebody's wishing their
shots fired a little faster.

174
00:08:05,787 --> 00:08:06,968
Which side am I on?

175
00:08:07,448 --> 00:08:08,261
Is it this one?

176
00:08:09,463 --> 00:08:10,467
Peek-a-boo!

177
00:08:10,770 --> 00:08:11,712
[agrunt moans]

178
00:08:11,712 --> 00:08:15,790
Okay, let's see what's so important
they were putting up all these defenses.

179
00:08:15,790 --> 00:08:17,464
Is that the exit back there?

180
00:08:17,464 --> 00:08:19,868
They've got it blocked off;
that must mean something.

181
00:08:20,564 --> 00:08:21,000
Wuah...

182
00:08:21,774 --> 00:08:24,156
What the hell?! It's just a corner!

183
00:08:24,156 --> 00:08:27,885
Fuck you and your stupid... webbing... shit!

184
00:08:27,885 --> 00:08:29,767
There's not a damned thing here!

185
00:08:30,718 --> 00:08:32,929
Oh, wait, there's one of these air things.

186
00:08:32,929 --> 00:08:35,522
Maybe there's an entrance up in the rafters?

187
00:08:35,522 --> 00:08:40,133
Well, there is an indentation.
Let me check, that might be it!

188
00:08:41,136 --> 00:08:43,034
No! There's nothing!

189
00:08:43,034 --> 00:08:45,734
If I jump on that, all I'm going
to do is brain myself.

190
00:08:46,225 --> 00:08:50,114
That's a lot of fighting I did just
to clear out a worthless dead end.

191
00:08:50,114 --> 00:08:54,392
I thought for sure this was the way
since the aliens clogged it up so much.

192
00:08:54,392 --> 00:08:56,574
This wouldn't be an issue if I had a map.

193
00:08:56,574 --> 00:09:00,381
Shouldn't there be fire exit
maps around here periodically?

194
00:09:00,381 --> 00:09:03,631
I haven't seen anything and I've
been doing a lot of wandering.

195
00:09:03,631 --> 00:09:06,878
So, what's the plan now?
Everything here is a dead end!

196
00:09:06,878 --> 00:09:09,947
Do I really want to try and go back
and dig through that fallen rock?

197
00:09:09,947 --> 00:09:13,560
Not that it will matter because
it's pressed up against a steel door.

198
00:09:13,560 --> 00:09:15,838
"Stop". Oh, thanks, THANKS!

199
00:09:15,838 --> 00:09:17,534
Now I know what to do.

200
00:09:21,026 --> 00:09:24,744
If I'm trapped down here long enough,
I'm going to have to start eating the aliens

201
00:09:24,744 --> 00:09:27,000
and I don't know how I'm going to cook them.

